<worksheet >
    <title>EIPO-3 Inner Products</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, complete all three problems. 
      Complete part c and one other part to earn a P.</p>
  </introduction>  
   <page>
      <exercise>
        <introduction>
            <p>Let <m>V = C[0, \infty)</m> be the space of continuous functions on the interval <m>[0, \infty)</m> with the weighted inner product defined by <m>\langle f, g \rangle = \int_{0}^{\infty} f(x)g(x)e^{-x} \, dx</m>.</p>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>If <m>f(x) = x</m> and <m>g(x) = 1</m>, evaluate the inner product <m>\langle f, g \rangle</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Compute the norm <m>\|f\|</m> of the function <m>f(x) = x</m>.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
        <task workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>Determine whether this integral converges for all continuous functions, or if constraints must be placed on the growth rate of the functions to qualify as a valid inner product space.</p>
            </statement>
        </task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>